From: CarlosDLMC <delamorenacoco.carlos@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:26:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] output: desktop zoom around the cursor (zoom_by)

zoom_by F multiplies the focused monitor's zoom by F, kept within 1..10, as
Hyprland's cursor:zoom_factor (zoom_rigid off): the frame is magnified around
the cursor, the point under it stays put and the view stays on the output.
After the scene renders, a second pass draws that region of the frame over
the whole output. While zoomed the scene redraws whole frames and the cursor
is drawn in software, so it is magnified with them. The factor animates over
animation_duration_zoom (800 ms) on animation_curve_zoom (Hyprland's default
curve 0,0.75,0.15,1).
